WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.389 --> 00:00:02.279
Too often we focus all
of our attention and

00:00:02.279 --> 00:00:05.870
our resources on developing the most
senior people in the organization.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.347
If you haven't invested some of those
same resources in developing a pipe-line

00:00:09.347 --> 00:00:12.872
of talent, you may be disappointed when
people feel like they're not prepared to

00:00:12.872 --> 00:00:15.145
assume this significant
level of responsibility.

00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:21.050
[MUSIC]

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:24.736
What we're trying to do is provide a way
for people to get that kind of training or

00:00:24.736 --> 00:00:28.312
development a little earlier in their
careers, so that they can polish those

00:00:28.312 --> 00:00:31.806
skills and eventually grow into their
more senior leadership positions.

00:00:31.806 --> 00:00:37.696
&gt;&gt; Participants will gain an understanding
of the key concepts and fundamentals,

00:00:37.696 --> 00:00:44.103
such as finance, accounting, operations,
enabling them to make better decisions,

00:00:44.103 --> 00:00:48.795
become a greater asset to
the organization the day they return.

00:00:48.795 --> 00:00:53.550
&gt;&gt; I picked ELD because I want
to be an influential leader.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.220
&gt;&gt; It's more about the behavioral
aspect of being a leader,

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.950
inspiring your people, coping with change.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:05.980
&gt;&gt; Markets, laws are changing too quickly
to not take that time to stop and

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:10.250
reflect and focus on you, and what you
can learn, and what you can do better.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:15.280
&gt;&gt; The break that came
after the first module is

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.210
a good opportunity to reflect
on what you were doing well and

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.055
how you want to do it,
how you want to move forward.

00:01:23.055 --> 00:01:26.150
&gt;&gt; We help you take
what you learn here and

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:29.500
really implement it in your organization.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.297
&gt;&gt; It's very, very practical.

00:01:31.297 --> 00:01:33.980
The knowledge is easily implementable.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:41.212
&gt;&gt; I know I always have a resource I
can tap into, the tools, the framework.

00:01:41.212 --> 00:01:46.405
Even though I learn, I may forget, but
I know how to come back to find it.

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:49.771
&gt;&gt; The amount of takeaways I've gotten
from the other people talking about

00:01:49.771 --> 00:01:51.150
the things we've learned and

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.925
that's giving us just as much
as the sessions themselves.

00:01:53.925 --> 00:01:56.928
&gt;&gt; The design thinking,
the opportunity to come back,

00:01:56.928 --> 00:02:01.267
the focus on organizational behavior and
your own leadership style as well,

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:04.023
Stanford hasn't disappointed
on any of those.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:08.831
&gt;&gt; ELD, somebody said to me, at a scale
of 1 to 10, how would you rate it,

00:02:08.831 --> 00:02:10.163
and my answer 15.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:13.330
&gt;&gt; I returned to work with so
much more energy and positivity.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.310
I have a clearer plan in terms of
what I wanted to implement and

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:17.440
where I wanted to go.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.690
&gt;&gt; I'm excited, because I think it's
going to make me a better leader.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:23.888
&gt;&gt; I would recommend this program
to anyone who wants to move their

00:02:23.888 --> 00:02:27.465
organization, their own position,
their future to the next level.

00:02:27.465 --> 00:02:28.850
[MUSIC]

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.424
&gt;&gt; You just feel like, hey, I'm ready,

00:02:31.424 --> 00:02:34.633
ready to take on any
challenge without any fear.

00:02:34.633 --> 00:02:36.308
It's transformational.

00:02:36.308 --> 00:02:39.300
[MUSIC]

